{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:16:03Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 107, "kind": "message", "text": "The spec is written to `docs/spec.md`. Summary of the triage and scope:\n\n**Triage:** Feature, backend-only, single layer (the store) \u2014 no split needed.\n\n**Scope:** `TaskStore` gains disk-backed persistence \u2014 a synchronous full-snapshot write to `backend/data/tasks.json` on every mutation, and a load-on-construct step that starts empty on any failure (missing file, invalid JSON, or wrong shape), matching the request's \"corrupt or missing \u2192 start empty, never crash\" requirement.\n\n**Key decisions made (not left open), since each had a clear default:**\n- Data file path resolved relative to `store.py`'s own location, not cwd\n- An env var (`TASKS_DATA_FILE`) overrides the path \u2014 this is what lets `conftest.py` redirect tests to a tmp path *before* `app.main` is imported, so the existing test suite never touches the real data file\n- Next-id counter derived as `max(loaded ids) + 1` rather than persisted separately\n- `backend/data/` added to `.gitignore`\n\n**Non-goals called out explicitly:** no database, no file locking (single-process app), no partial recovery of corrupt files, no export/import endpoint, no frontend changes.\n\nThis is ready to hand to the ux-designer stage \u2014 though since there's no UI surface here, that stage should be a no-op and this can likely go straight to the developer. Let me know if you want me to continue the pipeline (ux-designer \u2192 developer \u2192 reviewer) or if you'd like to review the spec first.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "d09eb7f3-5b08-4bee-8f0c-9efa0bcf1ce8"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:16:03Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 108, "kind": "status", "text": "The spec is written to `docs/spec.md`. Summary of the triage and scope:\n\n**Triage:** Feature, backend-only, single layer (the store) \u2014 no split needed.\n\n**Scope:** `TaskStore` gains disk-backed persistence \u2014 a synchronous full-snapshot write to `backend/data/tasks.json` on every mutation, and a load-on-construct step that starts empty on any failure (missing file, invalid JSON, or wrong shape), matching the request's \"corrupt or missing \u2192 start empty, never crash\" requirement.\n\n**Key decisions made (not left open), since each had a clear default:**\n- Data file path resolved relative to `store.py`'s own location, not cwd\n- An env var (`TASKS_DATA_FILE`) overrides the path \u2014 this is what lets `conftest.py` redirect tests to a tmp path *before* `app.main` is imported, so the existing test suite never touches the real data file\n- Next-id counter derived as `max(loaded ids) + 1` rather than persisted separately\n- `backend/data/` added to `.gitignore`\n\n**Non-goals called out explicitly:** no database, no file locking (single-process app), no partial recovery of corrupt files, no export/import endpoint, no frontend changes.\n\nThis is ready to hand to the ux-designer stage \u2014 though since there's no UI surface here, that stage should be a no-op and this can likely go straight to the developer. Let me know if you want me to continue the pipeline (ux-designer \u2192 developer \u2192 reviewer) or if you'd like to review the spec first.", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "d09eb7f3-5b08-4bee-8f0c-9efa0bcf1ce8", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.5476428000000001}}
